# Build context exclusions — load-bearing for gate G10, not housekeeping.
#
# Docker transfers the ENTIRE build context to the daemon before the first layer runs. This
# repository is ~1.2 GB on disk and the Dockerfile needs about 4 MB of it. Without this file
# every `docker build` shipped ~1.15 GB of caches, virtualenvs and deleted-file archives
# across the Docker Desktop virtualization boundary before anything compiled — a direct,
# measurable share of G10's 181.092 s against its 180 s threshold.
#
# It also fixed a correctness bug that had been passing by luck. `COPY frontend/ ./` runs
# AFTER `RUN npm ci`, so without `frontend/node_modules` excluded here, the host's macOS
# node_modules overwrote the container's freshly installed Linux one. The build succeeded
# only because the host tree happens to carry all 23 @esbuild platform variants, including
# linux-arm64, so esbuild still resolved a usable binary at runtime. `npm ci`'s entire
# output was being discarded, and the image carried every platform's binaries plus all
# devDependencies. **If you delete this file, that bug comes back silently.**

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Virtualenvs and dependency trees — rebuilt inside the image, never copied in
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
.venv/
.venv-review/
**/node_modules/
**/__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Tooling caches — pure waste in a build context
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.pytest_cache/
.import_linter_cache/
.hypothesis/
.benchmarks/
htmlcov/
.coverage

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Working directories and archives that are not the product
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
_to_delete/
_incoming/
ci-out/
gen/
*.tar.gz

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# VCS and CI metadata. The image never reads git history; `agentdx version` reads
# pyproject.toml, not `git describe`.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
.git/
.github/
.gitignore
.pre-commit-config.yaml

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Runtime data — a developer's local runs must never be baked into an image
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
.agentdx-data/
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Frontend build output and test artifacts. `vite build` regenerates dist/ inside stage 1;
# copying a host-built one in would ship whatever was last built locally.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
frontend/dist/
frontend/.vite/
frontend/test-results/
frontend/playwright-report/
src/agentdx/api/static/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Tests and benchmarks. The image runs the demo; it does not run the suite.
#
# `docs/` is deliberately NOT excluded. The Dockerfile copies `docs/openapi.json`, and
# excluding the directory would mean relying on a `!docs/openapi.json` re-inclusion — which
# works, but is the kind of ordering subtlety that breaks silently when someone reorders
# this file. docs/ is roughly a megabyte against the ~1.15 GB this file saves; buying
# robustness with that is the right trade.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
tests/
bench/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Session scratch — scripts and reports produced by build sessions, not by the product
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
*-plan.md
*-design.md
op2-*.md
op3-*.md
commit-*.sh
verify-*.sh
CONTEXT.md
AGENTS.md
CHANGELOG.md
CONTRIBUTING.md
